<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss Commission details 1996, 1997 forecast.</title>
<headline>Swiss Commission details 1996, 1997 forecast.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's Commission for Economic Policy issued the following forecast for 1996 and 1997. (Percentage changes compared with previous year):</p>
<p>					 1996	  1997</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product	  -0.7	  +0.5</p>
<p> Gross National Product	  -0.7	  +0.7</p>
<p> Private household consumption +0.25	 +0.25</p>
<p> Public sector consumption     -0.50	 -1.25</p>
<p> Construction investment	 -3.50	 -4.0</p>
<p> Fixed asset investment	  +5.0	  +3.0</p>
<p> Domestic demand		   -0.5	  +0.3</p>
<p> Exports			     +1.9	  +3.9</p>
<p> Imports			     +1.9	  +3.0</p>
<p> Unemployment rate, pct	  4.7	   5.2</p>
<p> Wages				 +1.4	  0.0</p>
<p> Disposable household income   0.0	   +0.5</p>
<p> Household savings rate, pct   9.7	   8.8</p>
<p> Central bank money		+3.5	  +2.0</p>
<p> Three-month Eurofrancs, pct   1.75	  1.50</p>
<p> Yield government bonds, pct   4.0	   3.75</p>
<p> Consumer price index	    +0.75	 +1.25</p>
<p> Unit wage costs		   +0.7	  -0.5</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
